---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<Base lang="en" page="privacy">
  <article class="prose">
    <p><em>Last updated: October 27, 2026</em></p>

    <h2>Person in charge of personal information</h2>
    <p>
      {site.founder.name}, {site.name}<br />
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> · <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a>
    </p>
    <p>Contact us with any question, to access or correct your information, or to withdraw your consent.</p>

    <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>When you call or email us:</strong> your name, contact details and the details of your request. We use
        them only to reply and to carry out the job.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your cookie choice:</strong> stored in your browser (local storage) so we don’t ask again. Nothing is sent
        to us.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Only if you click “Accept”:</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>Google Analytics 4: pages viewed, device and browser type, approximate city, how you reached the site. Used to measure site traffic.</li>
          <li>Google Ads: used to know whether an ad led to a call or an email, and to show our ads to people who visited the site.</li>
          <li>Meta Pixel (Facebook, Instagram): same purposes as Google Ads, on Meta’s platforms.</li>
        </ul>
        These tools set cookies and tell us when someone clicks our phone number or email address. They do not give us
        your name or contact details.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Hosting:</strong> the site is hosted on GitHub Pages, which keeps technical logs (IP address, date, page
        requested) to secure the service.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cookies: your consent</h2>
    <p>
      No analytics or advertising cookie is set before you agree. Rejecting is as easy as accepting, and the site works
      the same either way. You can change your mind at any time with the “Cookie preferences” link at the bottom of
      every page.
    </p>

    <h2>Transfers outside Quebec</h2>
    <p>
      Google, Meta and GitHub process data on servers outside Quebec, including in the United States. We do not sell
      any personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Google Analytics data is kept for 14 months. Client correspondence is kept as long as needed for the job and for
      accounting obligations.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask to access, correct or delete your information, and withdraw your consent. If you are not satisfied
      with our answer, you can file a complaint with the
      <a href="https://www.cai.gouv.qc.ca/" rel="noopener">Commission d’accès à l’information du Québec</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
